# ============================================================================
# FILE PURPOSE · What must never reach the remote repository.
#
# The critical rules are the POC data ones. Footage of real homes is personal
# data under UK GDPR, and a house inventory combined with a move date is a
# target list for burglary. Neither may be committed. See GAPS.md C5 and C6.
#
# Verified behaviour: poc/data/** and poc/ground_truth.csv are ignored, while
# the .gitkeep files, the notebook and the JSON tables stay tracked.
# ============================================================================

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- jupyter ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- POC data ---
# Footage of real homes is personal data under UK GDPR and must never be committed.
# A house inventory plus a move date is also a target list. See GAPS.md C5 / C6.
# Ignore ALL of poc/data — footage, dataset downloads, extracted frames.
# The HomeObjects-3K download alone is ~390MB of images.
poc/data/**
!poc/data/input/
!poc/data/input/.gitkeep
!poc/data/output/
!poc/data/output/.gitkeep

# Ground truth can carry property addresses — keep it local.
poc/ground_truth.csv

# Sweep output. One JSON per run, can hold thousands of measurement rows.
# Everything a run writes, not just the JSON: run_combination now also saves
# annotated frames and items.csv into poc/results/<run>/. Those JPEGs embed the
# input photograph, so with a dataset input they would drag dataset imagery into
# git — which is precisely what poc/data/** exists to prevent.
poc/results/**
!poc/results/.gitkeep
poc/rnd/results/**
!poc/rnd/results/.gitkeep

# --- model weights & caches ---
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors
.cache/
hub/

# --- secrets ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Per-pipeline input and output. Each pipeline folder owns its own photographs and
# its own results; neither belongs in git. The annotated frames embed the input
# photograph, so with a dataset input they would drag dataset imagery in.
# NOTE the single '*', not '**'. `data/**` matches the data/input DIRECTORY and
# excludes it, and git will not descend into an excluded directory to re-include a
# file inside it — so data/input/.gitkeep silently vanished from the repo and a
# fresh clone had no input folder. Ignoring the CONTENTS keeps the folder itself.
poc/pipelines/*/data/input/*
!poc/pipelines/*/data/input/.gitkeep
poc/pipelines/*/results/*
!poc/pipelines/*/results/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLIENT-CONFIDENTIAL AND COMMERCIAL MATERIAL — never on GitHub.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. The files below are a named client's commercial and
# proposal material, not research code:
#
#   estimation/   the effort estimate — module-by-module man-days, phase totals,
#                 scope options and the risk register. This is BJIT's pricing basis
#                 for a specific client and must not be published.
#   design/       the proposal diagram pack shared with the client.
#   SYSTEM-DESIGN.md    marked internal in its own header: "do not paste it into a
#                       client deck". Publishing it contradicts the document.
#   AI-CORE-DESIGN.md   the client-facing architecture write-up.
#
# Gitignore is enough ONLY because none of these were ever committed. If any had
# been tracked, ignoring it would not remove it — that needs `git rm --cached`, and
# the content would still sit in history.
#
# If this repo is ever made private, delete this block rather than working around it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
estimation/
design/
SYSTEM-DESIGN.md
AI-CORE-DESIGN.md
